📄 Week 6 Report – Web Security & Vulnerability Testing

🔐 This report documents my Week 6 Cybersecurity Internship practical work, focused on Web Security and Vulnerability Assessment & Penetration Testing (VAPT) basics. The report covers hands-on security testing performed in a controlled local lab environment using DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application), Burp Suite Community Edition, and OWASP ZAP.

🧪 During this week, I explored common web application vulnerabilities, including SQL Injection and Cross-Site Scripting (XSS). I performed both Reflected XSS and Stored XSS testing on DVWA and analyzed how vulnerable inputs can affect web applications.

🌐 I also used Burp Suite to intercept and examine HTTP requests and responses, gaining practical understanding of web traffic, parameters, headers, and security testing workflows.

🛡️ Using OWASP ZAP, I performed an automated vulnerability scan against the DVWA application and analyzed the identified security issues, including missing security headers and server information disclosure.

📊 The report includes the testing methodology, tools and technologies used, practical screenshots, vulnerability findings, risk levels, security implications, mitigation techniques, challenges faced, solutions implemented, and key learning outcomes.

🎯 Overall, this week helped me strengthen my practical understanding of web application security, VAPT methodologies, vulnerability identification, HTTP traffic analysis, and security hardening techniques through a safe and controlled cybersecurity lab environment.
